From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:32:43 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0998): reject malformed config files on import

Whole-product review finding 10. --import-config read both source files
with load_path, so a malformed newer *2.toml became default (empty)
options, passed validation and replaced the valid server options.

The import now uses hbb_common's try_load_path (patch hbb_common 0802)
and rejects a source file that does not parse, an options file that is
empty, and one whose options did not all survive parsing (Config2's
field deserializers turn a wrongly typed value into a default). Both
files are still validated before either destination is written. A
missing options file is still allowed.

Test: remotesmith::setup::tests::malformed_import_is_rejected.

Numbered 0998 (outside unit C2's 0800-0899 range) because
src/remotesmith/setup.rs only exists once 0990 has moved the module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
